 "sentences": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "text": "Why Don't Airplanes Fall Out of the Sky?",
   "start": 0.06,
   "end": 2.43,
   "firstWord": 0,
   "lastWord": 7
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "text": "Right now, thousands of people are flying through the sky inside giant metal machines.",
   "start": 3.27,
   "end": 8.82,
   "firstWord": 8,
   "lastWord": 21
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "text": "Some of these planes weigh hundreds of tons.",
   "start": 9.09,
   "end": 11.67,
   "firstWord": 22,
   "lastWord": 29
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "text": "So why don't they simply fall?",
   "start": 11.97,
   "end": 13.92,
   "firstWord": 30,
   "lastWord": 35
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "text": "And here's the surprising part: it's not the engines that hold them up.",
   "start": 14.34,
   "end": 18.33,
   "firstWord": 36,
   "lastWord": 48
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "text": "To understand why, imagine sticking your hand out of a moving car window.",
   "start": 18.75,
   "end": 23.22,
   "firstWord": 49,
   "lastWord": 61
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "text": "Tilt it slightly, and you'll feel the air pushing your hand upward.",
   "start": 23.58,
   "end": 27.36,
   "firstWord": 62,
   "lastWord": 73
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "text": "An airplane wing works on a similar principle, but on a much bigger scale.",
   "start": 27.72,
   "end": 32.07,
   "firstWord": 74,
   "lastWord": 87
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "text": "As the airplane moves forward, air flows around its wings.",
   "start": 32.49,
   "end": 36.21,
   "firstWord": 88,
   "lastWord": 97
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "text": "Their shape and angle change how the air moves, creating a difference in pressure.",
   "start": 36.57,
   "end": 41.31,
   "firstWord": 98,
   "lastWord": 111
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "text": "Typically, the pressure above the wing is lower than the pressure below it.",
   "start": 41.73,
   "end": 45.6,
   "firstWord": 112,
   "lastWord": 124
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "text": "This helps create an upward force called lift.",
   "start": 45.99,
   "end": 49.02,
   "firstWord": 125,
   "lastWord": 132
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "text": "But there's another way to understand what's happening.",
   "start": 49.47,
   "end": 51.81,
   "firstWord": 133,
   "lastWord": 140
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "text": "The wing pushes a huge amount of air downward.",
   "start": 52.2,
   "end": 55.17,
   "firstWord": 141,
   "lastWord": 149
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "text": "And according to Newton's third law, when the wing pushes air down, the air pushes the wing up.",
   "start": 55.47,
   "end": 61.32,
   "firstWord": 150,
   "lastWord": 167
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "text": "These are two ways of describing the same physical process.",
   "start": 61.74,
   "end": 65.34,
   "firstWord": 168,
   "lastWord": 177
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "text": "But there's a catch.",
   "start": 65.79,
   "end": 66.78,
   "firstWord": 178,
   "lastWord": 181
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "text": "For the wings to produce enough lift, air needs to flow past them at sufficient speed.",
   "start": 67.17,
   "end": 72.27,
   "firstWord": 182,
   "lastWord": 197
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "text": "That's why airplanes accelerate along the runway before taking off.",
   "start": 72.63,
   "end": 76.41,
   "firstWord": 198,
   "lastWord": 207
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "text": "So what are the engines actually doing?",
   "start": 76.86,
   "end": 79.35,
   "firstWord": 208,
   "lastWord": 214
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "text": "They create thrust, which helps the airplane overcome air resistance and maintain speed.",
   "start": 79.71,
   "end": 85.08,
   "firstWord": 215,
   "lastWord": 227
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "text": "And now, the most surprising question.",
   "start": 85.65,
   "end": 88.05,
   "firstWord": 228,
   "lastWord": 233
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "text": "What happens if both engines suddenly stop?",
   "start": 88.44,
   "end": 91.11,
   "firstWord": 234,
   "lastWord": 240
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "text": "Does the airplane fall?",
   "start": 91.47,
   "end": 92.7,
   "firstWord": 241,
   "lastWord": 244
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "text": "Not immediately.",
   "start": 93.15,
   "end": 94.14,
   "firstWord": 245,
   "lastWord": 246
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "text": "It can keep gliding, using altitude to maintain forward speed while the wings continue producing lift.",
   "start": 94.5,
   "end": 100.8,
   "firstWord": 247,
   "lastWord": 262
  },
  {
   "i": 26,
   "text": "That's right. A passenger jet can temporarily fly without engine power.",
   "start": 101.16,
   "end": 105.81,
   "firstWord": 263,
   "lastWord": 273
  },
  {
   "i": 27,
   "text": "So next time you see an airplane overhead, remember:",
   "start": 106.2,
   "end": 109.5,
   "firstWord": 274,
   "lastWord": 282
  },
  {
   "i": 28,
   "text": "It's not magic holding hundreds of tons in the sky.",
   "start": 109.86,
   "end": 113.16,
   "firstWord": 283,
   "lastWord": 292
  },
  {
   "i": 29,
   "text": "It's invisible air, working with the laws of physics.",
   "start": 113.55,
   "end": 116.97,
   "firstWord": 293,
   "lastWord": 301
  }
 ],
